From 224fdf341896d75ed344301642d112cccf3dacc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 17:33:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 59/71] inline-3d(Phase 1): carry layer identity from cc
 through the aggregator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The inline-3D weave has always joined a tracked element rect to the quad
that draws its pixels GEOMETRICALLY — best-overlap between the element's
screen rect and a root-pass resource quad's rect. That is a guess, and it
guesses wrong exactly when it matters: during a fast scroll the tracked
rect trails the impl transform, several quads clear the overlap bar at
once, and the weave picks the wrong one (browser#22's blown-up header,
browser#28's mismatched exclusions).

cc already knows the answer. A tracked element rect is collected FROM a
LayerImpl, and that same LayerImpl stamps its
stable_id_for_shared_quad_state() into every SharedQuadState it
populates. Carry that id along with the rect and the join becomes an
equality test instead of an overlap score.

This patch is the plumbing only — nothing consumes the identity yet:

  - viz::TrackedElementRect gains `sqs_layer_id` (uint32, default 0),
    over mojom + traits, with the round-trip unittest and the fuzz
    domain extended. It is deliberately NOT a constructor argument: it
    is a compositor-side annotation, never something a producer supplies.
  - LayerTreeHostImpl::CollectTrackedElementRects stamps it. The comment
    there records the one thing a consumer must not get wrong: the
    stable id is per-LayerImpl-INSTANCE and re-established every frame,
    so it is a within-frame join key and never a persistent identifier.
  - SurfaceAggregator::RootResourceQuad records the other half of the
    join: the aggregated SharedQuadState's layer_id, the per-client
    layer_namespace_id (a layer id is only unique within one client, so
    the PAIR is the key), and the quad's ordinal in the recording order
    — root-pass paint order, which the exclusion work needs for z.
  - SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects takes the client
    namespace id; both call sites already had it to hand.

`sqs_layer_id == 0` means "unstamped" — the legacy metadata channel, the
TreesInViz layer-context channel, or an older renderer — and every
consumer built on this must treat it as "no identity, fall back to
geometry".

